From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vgauthImport: use the arguments left after option parsing

main() copies argc/argv, lets g_option_context_parse() consume the options
from the copy, and then checks the original argc and passes the original
argv[1] on. The copy and the original share one array, which the parser
rewrites, so `vmware-alias-import -v` passes a NULL namespace and crashes:

  #0  __strlen_avx2 () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6
  #1  DynBuf_AppendString ()
  #2  main ()

Check and use what the parser left in the copy.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 open-vm-tools/vgauthImport/vgauthImport.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/open-vm-tools/vgauthImport/vgauthImport.c b/open-vm-tools/vgauthImport/vgauthImport.c
--- a/open-vm-tools/vgauthImport/vgauthImport.c
+++ b/open-vm-tools/vgauthImport/vgauthImport.c
@@ -568,12 +568,12 @@ main(int argc, char *argv[])
       goto out;
    }
 
-   if (argc < 2) {
+   if (argcCopy < 2) {
       PrintUsage(optCtx);
       goto out;
    }
 
-   success = ProcessNamespace(argv[1], ctx) ? 0 : 1;
+   success = ProcessNamespace(argvCopy[1], ctx) ? 0 : 1;
 
 out:
    if (NULL != ctx) {
-- 
2.53.0

